<code>assert index >= 0 && index < this.size() && role != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement captures the condition that if the index is within bounds and the role is not null, then for every index `i` less than the given index, the element at `i` remains unchanged. Specifically, it checks that if the element at `i` was null before, it remains null, and if it was not null before, it remains equal to its previous value.
